      },
      "description": 
"Collect merge-request-based standup data from the GitLab or GitHub account the user linked to this connector. Returns one JSON object: \`today\`, \`previousDays[]\` with the events of each, \`todayEvents[]\`, \`myMrs[]\` bucketed ready / blocked / draft / stale, \`reviews[]\` waiting on the user, and \`blockers[]\` carrying the error lines read out of each failed pipeline job log.

Call it once at the start of a working day, to write a standup note. It is a snapshot, not a search API: it cannot fetch one named merge request, reach further back than the previous working day, or filter by project.

Read-only. Credentials come from the accounts linked on the connect page, never from an argument. With one linked account no argument is needed; with several, pass \`provider\` or \`host\` — an ambiguous call fails and lists the linked accounts, so ask the user which one they mean. An expired login fails with a request to reconnect the connector."
,
      "inputKeys": [
